| Conversion | Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |

## An Admin has every staff page

An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.
## Two records of one person

When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: "Your CarmaCars accounts are now one". A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and **Merge into this record** under the renter still works as before.

1. Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.
2. Two different people after all? Press **Undo** and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.

## New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal

Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: their staff agreement first, then the academy, then everything else (release 48: the agreement moved before the academy; anyone who already passed the academy is only asked to sign). Until the agreement is signed they open only **Welcome**, their profile, the guide and their documents to sign; after it, until the academy is passed, only the academy, the guide, their profile and Welcome.

1. The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire''s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.
2. **Team** > **Staff and roles**, **Staff agreements**: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire''s licence number), and **Waive** with the reason.
3. Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the agreement and the academy are done, shows the team''s WhatsApp group (Program settings, **WhatsApp team group link** and **WhatsApp Sales group link**; empty until you set them: while either is empty, Hiring warns and To do keeps an urgent task. Reset the invite link in WhatsApp, keep Add other members for admins only and Approve new participants on, then paste it). Each group shows the person''s member tag ("Name - Position") with Copy and the steps; I joined needs **I set my member tag**. The same link goes by email, once.

## Accounts locked for inactivity

A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, **Staff inactive lock days**) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees "Account locked for inactivity" when they sign in. You get an alert. On **Team** > **Staff and roles** the row says **Locked for inactivity**: press **Unlock**. The staff list shows each person''s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.

## Hours and the townhall

**Team** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.

**Breaks and idle time (release 35).** Customer service, Fleet and Finance press **Start break** and **End break** next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On **Timesheet**, each person''s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. **Edit** or **Remove** a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is **Program settings** > va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period''s breaks).

While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, "Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min", and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with **Set Quo user** on Timesheet; the **Call** button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. **KPIs** shows **Idle minutes** against kpi_idle_minutes_week.

**Team** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 6:30 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week''s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; **Build again** refreshes the numbers. With no call link in Program settings, **Join the call** opens the call in the site; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.

## The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)

1. The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time. To change it, press **Change the day or time** on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website''s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants'' live calls always take the hour before.
2. Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. **Join the call** on the townhall page, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.
3. When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows "Missed N townhalls" for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.
4. The deck''s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role''s numbers for the week. Press **Add a shout-out** on a tile to add yours.

## Where staff live (release 35)

Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.

## Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)

- New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the staff agreement, the academy, confirming the team''s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.
- Each person''s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example "Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature". **Mark WhatsApp joined** records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the agreement and the academy are done, **Confirm WhatsApp and approve** marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).
- Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today''s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.
- Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.
- Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person''s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).
- Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.
- Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.
- Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.
- A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.
- Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.
- The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.

## Work chats only

All staff work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. It is in every staff guide and in the academy (Work chats). Answer a private work message in the group.

## Staff rewards (release 48)

1. **People** > **Team** > **Staff rewards** lists every staff member: whether they get rental perks and why not, their tier, their progress, their free days and what they used.
2. Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. Remote and international staff get none. Use **Perks** to switch one person on or off by hand, with the reason they read.
3. From day one (the academy and the agreement done): 15% off their own rentals. Sales earn 1 free day per 100 rental days booked, Field 1 per 100 handovers. Silver at 50 rental days booked in a month is 20% off; Gold at 100 is 25% off and 1 bonus free day. The month''s top seller gets a free weekend.
4. A perk rental is picked up within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter asked for, never on exotic or partner cars, and the staff member must be the driver. A free day ends after 6 months. A suspended account''s perks are frozen.
5. Free days go on CarmaCars'' and shareholders'' cars first. On a co-host owner''s car the owner is paid as at the full rate. Each perk used is posted as a staff benefit expense (account 5300).
6. **Add free days** gives a person free days by hand, with the reason. Every number is in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Staff rewards**.
## Data to check on each record (release 48)

Every portal checks the person''s own record and shows them a box with the fix: Settings > Staff, Owners and Renters (renters with a booking in the last 90 days) list everyone with something open, in words. **Send reminder** sends a staff member an alert; an owner or a renter sees the box again at their next page, even a warning they put off. A blocking item (the staff agreement waiting for the licence number or the home address, an expired licence of someone who drives) cannot be put off. In-person staff with a home address outside Ontario are asked to confirm it with the reason; what they wrote is kept.

## Updated agreements to accept (release 48)

When a document changes (the terms of use, the privacy policy, the rental agreement, the owner program agreement, the staff agreements), everyone it binds sees one box at their next sign-in: what changed in a few lines, the new text, and **Accept and continue**. Accepting is recorded with the version, the time, the IP address and the device; nobody signs again. Declining keeps their portal closed and shows how to reach us. Admin settings, Terms, lists each version with how many accepted, declined or still wait, and who.

Release 48 published three: the rental agreement (the new return charges), the owner program agreement (owner use for someone else, the $150 Install Fee) and the staff agreements (confidentiality, non-solicitation for 12 months, data returned or deleted on exit, and a non-compete for contractors only: none for employees, as Ontario''s Employment Standards Act requires).

## People on the live map

The live map (Visitors, and Cars > Fleet tracking) has a **People** layer: staff on shift or on a job, and renters and owners at a pickup or return, each with a marker by role. Use the role chips to show or hide each group. Staff appear only after they accept the electronic monitoring policy, and never off duty; renters and owners only with their phone''s permission and only two hours either side of a pickup or return. Only the latest position is kept, plus a job''s points for 30 days. Admins and Fleet see everyone; customer service and Sales see renters at a pickup or return; Finance and field staff see no one.

## Resignations (release 50)

Staff resign themselves on their **Profile** (**Resign**, the last section; on **Welcome** while still in onboarding). You get an email and an alert, Finance too, and an Offboarding To do opens in the Admin queue.

**People** > **Staff and roles** shows **Resigning: last day** with the day notice was given, the reason and the **Offboarding To do** link. After the last day it shows Resigned, with the dates.

1. The To do lists what to do: final pay up to the last day (Finance), the keys, cards and equipment to collect (not tracked in the system), their open field jobs and shifts to reassign, and the leads, chats, To dos and claims to hand back.
2. Their field jobs and shifts after the last day go back to the queue at once; nobody can give them a shift or a job after it.
3. **Change last day** moves it earlier or later (from today); they are emailed the new day and the To do follows. **Withdraw resignation** cancels it for them. **End access now** ends it at once.
4. After the last day their access ends by itself (the same as **End access**), their open To dos and chats go back to the queues and their claims are released. **Restore** gives access back if they return.
5. Someone who resigned by email or in person: **Record a resignation** on their row, with the last day and the reason as they gave it. Today ends their access now.
6. The connector''s `list_staff` shows each person''s resignation.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.</p><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-portals-and-sign-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Portals and sign-in</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Portals and view as</b>. Every portal has a card.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each card links to <b class="gd-ui">Its sign-in page</b>, the address to send that person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a person in the list on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open as this person</b> to see that portal as they see it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The site&#39;s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend&#39;s test inboxes) are marked &quot;Test account&quot; in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:65.9%;top:30.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:58.1%;top:39.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.6%;top:45.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-invite-a-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Invite a person</h2><p class="gd-p">Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Name and Email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>. The link in the email works for 24 hours.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/360"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="360"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:66.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.8%;top:87.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People &gt; Owners and People &gt; Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-add-an-investor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add an investor</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add an investor</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer&#39;s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Invite now is ticked: press <b class="gd-ui">Add and invite</b>. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-send-a-password-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send a password link</h2><p class="gd-p">For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On their row, press <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>. They get &quot;Reset your CarmaCars password&quot;, valid for 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> on the same row opens their portal, read only.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/440"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="440"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.8%;top:6.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.2%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.1%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-view-as-see-what-someone-sees" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">View as: see what someone sees</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A red banner says &quot;Viewing as Name (email), read only.&quot; on every page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Exit</b> to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/620"><img src="/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="620"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Can&#39;t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-audit-log" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The audit log</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Logs</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Changes</b> tab, shows who changed what, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Search by table, record id or value.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/audit</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.6%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:39%;top:46.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.6%;top:20.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-and-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff and roles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> opens Staff and roles.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row has <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">End access</b> to close their staff portal at once. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> undoes it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/780"><img src="/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="780"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:59%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:86.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:92.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-admin-access" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Admin access</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site&#39;s nightly checks sign in with.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change the list only if the business&#39;s Admin address changes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-scorecards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff scorecards</h2><p class="gd-p">See how each assistant is doing against the targets.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/350"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="350"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.1%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales by staff member</h2><p class="gd-p">See each person&#39;s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> or <b class="gd-ui">By month</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Commission rate</b> gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. <b class="gd-ui">Home address</b> here changes it if it is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The whole team: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to</td><td>Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-staff-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales staff: in person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Work mode</b> on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month&#39;s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a remote person&#39;s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rates</td><td>In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Remote minimum</td><td>400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings &gt; Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-an-admin-has-every-staff-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An Admin has every staff page</h2><p class="gd-p">An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-two-records-of-one-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Two records of one person</h2><p class="gd-p">When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: &quot;Your CarmaCars accounts are now one&quot;. A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> under the renter still works as before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Two different people after all? Press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-new-staff-the-academy-then-the-agreement-then-the-portal" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: their staff agreement first, then the academy, then everything else (release 48: the agreement moved before the academy; anyone who already passed the academy is only asked to sign). Until the agreement is signed they open only <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>, their profile, the guide and their documents to sign; after it, until the academy is passed, only the academy, the guide, their profile and Welcome.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire&#39;s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Staff agreements</b>: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire&#39;s licence number), and <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the agreement and the academy are done, shows the team&#39;s WhatsApp group (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp team group link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp Sales group link</b>; empty until you set them: while either is empty, Hiring warns and To do keeps an urgent task. Reset the invite link in WhatsApp, keep Add other members for admins only and Approve new participants on, then paste it). Each group shows the person&#39;s member tag (&quot;Name - Position&quot;) with Copy and the steps; I joined needs <b class="gd-ui">I set my member tag</b>. The same link goes by email, once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-accounts-locked-for-inactivity" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Accounts locked for inactivity</h2><p class="gd-p">A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Staff inactive lock days</b>) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees &quot;Account locked for inactivity&quot; when they sign in. You get an alert. On <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> the row says <b class="gd-ui">Locked for inactivity</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b>. The staff list shows each person&#39;s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-hours-and-the-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hours and the townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Breaks and idle time (release 35).</b> Customer service, Fleet and Finance press <b class="gd-ui">Start break</b> and <b class="gd-ui">End break</b> next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>, each person&#39;s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period&#39;s breaks).</p><p class="gd-p">While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, &quot;Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min&quot;, and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with <b class="gd-ui">Set Quo user</b> on Timesheet; the <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Idle minutes</b> against kpi_idle_minutes_week.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 6:30 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week&#39;s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; <b class="gd-ui">Build again</b> refreshes the numbers. With no call link in Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens the call in the site; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-townhall-day-attendance-and-the-team-slide-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time. To change it, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the day or time</b> on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website&#39;s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants&#39; live calls always take the hour before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on the townhall page, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows &quot;Missed N townhalls&quot; for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The deck&#39;s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role&#39;s numbers for the week. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a shout-out</b> on a tile to add yours.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-where-staff-live-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where staff live (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-onboarding-breaks-and-shifts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the staff agreement, the academy, confirming the team&#39;s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin&#39;s or a Fleet VA&#39;s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.</li><li>Each person&#39;s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example &quot;Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature&quot;. <b class="gd-ui">Mark WhatsApp joined</b> records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the agreement and the academy are done, <b class="gd-ui">Confirm WhatsApp and approve</b> marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).</li><li>Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today&#39;s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.</li><li>Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.</li><li>Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person&#39;s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).</li><li>Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.</li><li>Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.</li><li>Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.</li><li>A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.</li><li>Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.</li><li>The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-work-chats-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work chats only</h2><p class="gd-p">All staff work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. It is in every staff guide and in the academy (Work chats). Answer a private work message in the group.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-rewards-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff rewards (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff rewards</b> lists every staff member: whether they get rental perks and why not, their tier, their progress, their free days and what they used.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. Remote and international staff get none. Use <b class="gd-ui">Perks</b> to switch one person on or off by hand, with the reason they read.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From day one (the academy and the agreement done): 15% off their own rentals. Sales earn 1 free day per 100 rental days booked, Field 1 per 100 handovers. Silver at 50 rental days booked in a month is 20% off; Gold at 100 is 25% off and 1 bonus free day. The month&#39;s top seller gets a free weekend.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A perk rental is picked up within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter asked for, never on exotic or partner cars, and the staff member must be the driver. A free day ends after 6 months. A suspended account&#39;s perks are frozen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Free days go on CarmaCars&#39; and shareholders&#39; cars first. On a co-host owner&#39;s car the owner is paid as at the full rate. Each perk used is posted as a staff benefit expense (account 5300).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add free days</b> gives a person free days by hand, with the reason. Every number is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff rewards</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-data-to-check-on-each-record-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Data to check on each record (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every portal checks the person&#39;s own record and shows them a box with the fix: Settings &gt; Staff, Owners and Renters (renters with a booking in the last 90 days) list everyone with something open, in words. <b class="gd-ui">Send reminder</b> sends a staff member an alert; an owner or a renter sees the box again at their next page, even a warning they put off. A blocking item (the staff agreement waiting for the licence number or the home address, an expired licence of someone who drives) cannot be put off. In-person staff with a home address outside Ontario are asked to confirm it with the reason; what they wrote is kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-updated-agreements-to-accept-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Updated agreements to accept (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When a document changes (the terms of use, the privacy policy, the rental agreement, the owner program agreement, the staff agreements), everyone it binds sees one box at their next sign-in: what changed in a few lines, the new text, and <b class="gd-ui">Accept and continue</b>. Accepting is recorded with the version, the time, the IP address and the device; nobody signs again. Declining keeps their portal closed and shows how to reach us. Admin settings, Terms, lists each version with how many accepted, declined or still wait, and who.</p><p class="gd-p">Release 48 published three: the rental agreement (the new return charges), the owner program agreement (owner use for someone else, the $150 Install Fee) and the staff agreements (confidentiality, non-solicitation for 12 months, data returned or deleted on exit, and a non-compete for contractors only: none for employees, as Ontario&#39;s Employment Standards Act requires).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-people-on-the-live-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">People on the live map</h2><p class="gd-p">The live map (Visitors, and Cars &gt; Fleet tracking) has a <b class="gd-ui">People</b> layer: staff on shift or on a job, and renters and owners at a pickup or return, each with a marker by role. Use the role chips to show or hide each group. Staff appear only after they accept the electronic monitoring policy, and never off duty; renters and owners only with their phone&#39;s permission and only two hours either side of a pickup or return. Only the latest position is kept, plus a job&#39;s points for 30 days. Admins and Fleet see everyone; customer service and Sales see renters at a pickup or return; Finance and field staff see no one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-resignations-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Resignations (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff resign themselves on their <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Resign</b>, the last section; on <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b> while still in onboarding). You get an email and an alert, Finance too, and an Offboarding To do opens in the Admin queue.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Resigning: last day</b> with the day notice was given, the reason and the <b class="gd-ui">Offboarding To do</b> link. After the last day it shows Resigned, with the dates.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The To do lists what to do: final pay up to the last day (Finance), the keys, cards and equipment to collect (not tracked in the system), their open field jobs and shifts to reassign, and the leads, chats, To dos and claims to hand back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Their field jobs and shifts after the last day go back to the queue at once; nobody can give them a shift or a job after it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change last day</b> moves it earlier or later (from today); they are emailed the new day and the To do follows. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw resignation</b> cancels it for them. <b class="gd-ui">End access now</b> ends it at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">After the last day their access ends by itself (the same as <b class="gd-ui">End access</b>), their open To dos and chats go back to the queues and their claims are released. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> gives access back if they return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Someone who resigned by email or in person: <b class="gd-ui">Record a resignation</b> on their row, with the last day and the reason as they gave it. Today ends their access now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The connector&#39;s <span class="gd-url">list_staff</span> shows each person&#39;s resignation.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'hiring', 'chapter', 'referral-partners-and-rentalcoverage', 'Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role''s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.

## Open a role and send the apply link

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links.

1. Press **Open the role** to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); **Close the role** takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.
2. Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.
3. Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role''s questions, about five minutes.
4. **Pass mark and pay** changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.

## What happens to each application

The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.

- Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).
- Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so. The email''s button is **Yes, put me in Sales**: one press makes their Sales application from the one they sent (no new form) and sends the AI interview link at once.
- Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.
- A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.
- Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.

## Review the applications

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Applications.

1. Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.
2. **Invite anyway** sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. **Decline** sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).
3. A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.

## Interview days

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Interview days.

1. Press **Add an interview day**: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).
2. Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate''s email and on their page.
3. Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.
4. **Turn off** stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.

## Run the calls with the rubric

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Calls.

1. Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press **Start**.
2. The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.
3. Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press **Save the rubric**. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.

## Shortlist and Hire

**People** > **Hiring**, tab Shortlist.

1. Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.
2. Open the candidate and press **Hire**. A short form opens: the **Role** (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the **Start date** and the **Pay**, filled in with the role''s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.
3. Press **Confirm: hire and start onboarding**. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do''s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email (release 44: no start date in it; training and claiming shifts only, then a hello in the team chat and the member tag "Name - Position" in each WhatsApp group, also a first-day To do); their call slot and AI interview link close.
4. The **Onboarding** card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire''s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press **Send the agreement**. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press **Verify**. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.
5. **Not hired** closes a candidate after the call without an email; **Withdrawn** is for one who no longer wants the role.

> Good to know: Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.


> Good to know: A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows "N applicants invited but no interview day is open for" the role, with **Add an interview day**. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time ("No call times are open right now"), get "New times are open" when the day is added.

## Decisions and the emails they send

The rubric''s **Decision** is Hire, Maybe, No, **Good fit for Sales instead** or No show. Recording one sends nothing.

1. **Good fit for Sales instead** refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.
2. Open **Hiring**, **Emails to send**: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.
3. **Change** a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or **Undo** it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).
4. Press **Send all decision emails**. Choose **Now**, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press **Hire** on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.

## AI interviews for the remote roles

Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. **People** > **Hiring**, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: **Turn off** sends the remote roles the booking link again. **Interview settings**: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).

1. The candidate gets one email, **Start my interview**. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.
2. They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role''s rubric: experience, the role''s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role''s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Every answer is on video and spoken, nothing is typed, and the English question is spoken too. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.
3. When the last answer is in, the candidate is **Interviewed**. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, scores every answer out of 10 with a one-line reason, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: **Invite to a live call**, **Hire**, **Decline** or **Good fit for Sales instead**. Hiring shows "N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision".
4. Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript, the AI''s score for that rubric line and the answer''s score out of 10. **Watch all** plays every video one after the other.
5. The interview decides by itself (release 41, on by default again since release 44): a pass needs all of these: the score at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in **Interview settings**), no knock-out answer, the answers averaging 7 or more out of 10 with none under 5, and spoken English judged good or fluent. A Sales applicant who passes is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy. Every other role that passes (customer service, fleet, finance and field) is invited to book an interview date. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press **Invite to a live call** on any candidate.
6. A link that expired: **New interview link** emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.

> Good to know: You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. **Interview settings** holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and **Decide by hand** if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings > Usage, "Hiring interviews"); when today''s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.

## Redo the AI interview

If an interview went badly for a reason that is not the applicant''s (a broken camera, a lost connection), open the candidate and press **Redo the AI interview**, then confirm.

1. Their staff access ends if they were already hired.
2. The old interview and its answers are kept as history on the candidate.
3. The application goes back to **Invited** and a new interview link is emailed, good for 7 days.

A redone interview follows the same pass rule as any other: only a Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself.

## Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed

- The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day''s **How** is only the default shown.
- Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with **Confirm my call** (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.
- **Calls** shows **Confirmed**, **Waiting** or **Asked 24 hours before** for each remote call, and **Cancelled: not confirmed** for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.

## Hire from any stage (release 35)
**Hire** is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: "<name> hired as <role>, starts <date>, training not started", which opens their academy progress.

## Every applicant into Sales

1. A closed role''s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.
2. The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.
3. Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.
4. A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview''s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.
5. The Hire form''s standard pay reads the role''s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.

## In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)

An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).

1. An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.
2. The list and the candidate page show **Lives in**, flag **Location mismatch** when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer **Move to Remote Sales** to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.
3. **Hire** chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.

## Interview dates before the townhall (release 35, widened in release 43)

Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 12:00 to 13:00), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on **Calls** here and on the Fleet home page.

## Interview call reminders (release 41)

For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day''s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or **Call** for a phone call). **Today** shows **Interviews today**: each call''s time, candidate, role and its **Join** or **Call** button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.

## The Sales funnel (release 48)

The Pipeline tab opens with **Sales funnel**.

1. **Sales staff in the academy**: how many have not started, are in progress or are done, and how many have made no progress for 2 days. Each person on the Academy step shows "Academy 3 of 19 (Sales), last active 2 days ago". A hired person with no academy progress is reminded on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email); the 5-day suspension follows.
2. **The re-send**: once, every applicant referred to Sales who never applied got the referral again as **Yes, put me in Sales**, and every Sales applicant who never finished the AI interview got a fresh link. One email per address, a few every 15 minutes.
3. **The bar for Sales**: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI''s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.
4. A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in **Settings** > **Program**.

## Interview calls in the site (release 50)

A video interview is now a private call inside the site, one room per slot, in place of the Jitsi link. The candidate''s booking email (with a calendar invite) has their own link: it opens the call in their browser with no account, and works in one browser only (another browser is refused; a moved or cancelled call''s link stops working). Opening the candidate yourself never uses their link: on the candidate''s page press **Join the interview call**. Their details, answers, the role''s questions and the rubric are beside the video, with **No show** and **Not hired**; Hire and the decision email stay on the candidate''s page.

The weekly townhall is a call in the site too (Townhall, **Join the call**): you present, your slide is everyone''s, and People shows who is in the call, who left and who has not joined. Attendance is recorded by itself. If the media server is down, **Switch to the outside link** on the Townhall page sends everyone to the link in Program settings until you switch back.', 'Hiring', 'Open roles and apply links for Indeed and OnlineJobs.ph, the applications and their scores, AI interviews for the remote roles, interview days, the rubric during each call, the ranked shortlist and Hire.',
