rd AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Every answer is on video and spoken, nothing is typed, and the English question is spoken too. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, scores every answer out of 10 with a one-line reason, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript, the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line and the answer&#39;s score out of 10. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The interview decides by itself (release 41, on by default again since release 44): a pass needs all of these: the score at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>), no knock-out answer, the answers averaging 7 or more out of 10 with none under 5, and spoken English judged good or fluent. A Sales applicant who passes is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy. Every other role that passes (customer service, fleet, finance and field) is invited to book an interview date. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b> on any candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b> holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and <b class="gd-ui">Decide by hand</b> if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-redo-the-ai-interview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Redo the AI interview</h2><p class="gd-p">If an interview went badly for a reason that is not the applicant&#39;s (a broken camera, a lost connection), open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Redo the AI interview</b>, then confirm.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Their staff access ends if they were already hired.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The old interview and its answers are kept as history on the candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The application goes back to <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b> and a new interview link is emailed, good for 7 days.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A redone interview follows the same pass rule as any other: only a Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-every-applicant-into-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every applicant into Sales</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A closed role&#39;s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview&#39;s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The Hire form&#39;s standard pay reads the role&#39;s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-in-person-needs-the-toronto-area-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list and the candidate page show <b class="gd-ui">Lives in</b>, flag <b class="gd-ui">Location mismatch</b> when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer <b class="gd-ui">Move to Remote Sales</b> to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-dates-before-the-townhall-release-35-widened-in-re" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview dates before the townhall (release 35, widened in release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 5:30 pm to 6:30 pm), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> here and on the Fleet home page. Interview call slots start at 5:30 pm Toronto time.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-call-reminders-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview call reminders (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day&#39;s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> for a phone call). <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Interviews today</b>: each call&#39;s time, candidate, role and its <b class="gd-ui">Join</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-the-sales-funnel-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Sales funnel (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">The Pipeline tab opens with <b class="gd-ui">Sales funnel</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sales staff in the academy</b>: how many have not started, are in progress or are done, and how many have made no progress for 2 days. Each person on the Academy step shows &quot;Academy 3 of 19 (Sales), last active 2 days ago&quot;. A hired person with no academy progress is reminded on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email); the 5-day suspension follows.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The re-send</b>: once, every applicant referred to Sales who never applied got the referral again as <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>, and every Sales applicant who never finished the AI interview got a fresh link. One email per address, a few every 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The bar for Sales</b>: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI&#39;s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-calls-in-the-site-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview calls in the site (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">A video interview is now a private call inside the site, one room per slot, in place of the Jitsi link. The candidate&#39;s booking email (with a calendar invite) has their own link: it opens the call in their browser with no account, and works in one browser only (another browser is refused; a moved or cancelled call&#39;s link stops working). Opening the candidate yourself never uses their link: on the candidate&#39;s page press <b class="gd-ui">Join the interview call</b>. Their details, answers, the role&#39;s questions and the rubric are beside the video, with <b class="gd-ui">No show</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b>; Hire and the decision email stay on the candidate&#39;s page.</p><p class="gd-p">The weekly townhall is a call in the site too (Townhall, <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b>): you present, your slide is everyone&#39;s, and People shows who is in the call, who left and who has not joined. Attendance is recorded by itself. If the media server is down, <b class="gd-ui">Switch to the outside link</b> on the Townhall page sends everyone to the link in Program settings until you switch back.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'academy', 'chapter', 'hiring', 'Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.

## Progress by staff member

1. Open **People** > **Academy**. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings > Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.
2. Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.
3. A section closed for them? Press **Open early**, give the reason and press **Open early** again. The reason is kept.

## Edit lessons and questions

1. Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.
2. **Edit the title** changes its name and what it covers.
3. Each lesson has **Preview** (the player) and **Edit the lesson**: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule; or a picture: a screen with numbered pins, a good and a bad photo side by side, a flow diagram, Do and Do not pairs or an icon list (each with its alt text). Every section ends with a lesson called **See it** of these pictures.
4. **Add a lesson**, **Delete** a lesson; each question has **Edit** (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and **Delete**; **Add a question** at the end. Every question also carries one funny wrong option (a joke, always wrong, never the right answer): it is added by itself when a question is saved, shows in the editor as "a joke, always wrong", and picking it scores nothing.

## The pass mark and the gate

- Settings > Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).
- Academy gate (on by default): a section opens only once the one before it is passed, and a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile (and Welcome). Every staff account is held until it passes: new hires from one-step Hire from the start, and the staff already working from release 34; their progress so far is kept. Admins are never held. Off: the academy only records progress.
- Release 33 added a section at the end of each path on what changed in releases 28 to 32 (bookings, handovers and returns; licences, photos and agreements; money; cars and listings), with its quiz.
- Take the Admin path yourself from **Take the Admin path**.

## The gate, Welcome and waivers (release 34)

- A new hire signs in to **Welcome**: four steps in order (welcome, their profile and phone, the academy, then their first-day tasks). While they are held, Welcome, the academy, the guide and their profile are all they open; any other page brings them back to Welcome.
- Each person''s progress is on their academy page (Admin > Academy, their name) and on their candidate page in Hiring, on the card **Academy gate**: held or open, and the sections passed.
- **Waive the academy** on that card opens their portal at once without the academy. Give the reason: it is kept in the audit log. **Take the waiver back** holds them again until they pass.
- Release 34 added four sections, each with its quiz: pickups and returns (check-in is the pickup, Sign and pay, Book it now, overrides), money (Charge the renter, holds, owner invoices paid outside the platform), listing photos from a shared folder, and the caller panel with renter notes. Staff who already passed see the new sections on their academy page; they are not held by them.
- Each section names the guide chapters it was written from. When one of those chapters is published again, the section is listed under **To review: the guide changed** on Admin > Academy: check its lessons and quiz against the guide, then press **Mark reviewed**.

## The quiz rules (release 35)

- A quiz passes at 90% (Program settings). The questions come in a random order and open only after the section''s reading time.
- After a failed try the person waits 30 minutes, and may take a quiz 3 times a day. Answers given too fast are flagged to the Admins.
- An Admin can reset chosen sections for one person.
- New sections for a role are added to its path. Staff who had already passed their path keep a week before the new sections hold them, and nothing they passed is reset.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

- Every staff role, and the Admin path, has the new path **The renter''s side**: one section for each step of the renter guide, each scene showing the renter''s screen and opening that page of the guide (staff read it at `/staff/guide/renter`, you at **Guides** > Renter).
- Each role''s path has a section of worked examples from its own guide chapters (customer service, Sales, Fleet, Finance, field work, Admin), with the guide''s screenshots and a quiz drawn from the examples.
- New hires are enrolled on The renter''s side by one-step Hire like every path and pass it before their portal opens. Staff already working who had passed everything have 7 days, shown on their academy page, before the new sections hold them; nothing is reset.
- A lesson scene can show a guide screenshot: in **Edit the lesson**, the picture `shot` with the chapter (for example `renter/sign-and-pay`), the image file and a line.
- **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel in every staff portal names the guide chapter of the page. When a staff question is not answered by the guide, add the answer in **Settings** > **Guides**.

## Guide me

Every staff portal has **Guide me** at the top: it walks the person through a real workflow while they do it, on the live screens (send an offer, answer a request, record a payment, a pickup, a return and deposit review, approve an owner''s car, a field expense). It is off by default; each person can keep it on from its menu. You have it too.

**Academy**, **Guide me: walkthroughs in the live screens**: for the last 30 days, each staff member''s walkthroughs started, completed and stopped, and for each workflow the step people stop at most.
', 'Academy', 'Training paths by function: progress, opening a section early, editing lessons and questions, the gate.',
