While you are clocked in and not on a break, the portal notes that you are active: a click, a key, a scroll or switching to its tab. It never records what you type, which pages you open or your screen. Keep the portal open in a tab while you work; a hidden tab nobody touches counts as inactive. After a few minutes without activity it asks **Still there?**: tap anywhere to carry on. Phone calls you take or make (your Quo user, the **Call** button or a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall count as active. Nothing is counted outside your scheduled hours.

## Your first days

Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first (sign it on Welcome or Documents to sign), then the academy, then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show your WhatsApp groups (Sales: CARMA Closers and the CarmaCars Team; everyone else the Team group). Next to each link is your member tag, written for you as "Name - Position" (for example "Darren - Sales"), with **Copy member tag** and the steps: open the group, tap its name, tap your own name (or Edit member tag), paste and save. Join each group and set the tag, then press **I joined** and tick **I set my member tag**: I joined does not go through without it.

Passed the Sales part of the academy while Sales is not your main role? Your home page shows the Sales group (CARMA Closers) too: join it and set your tag the same way.

No progress in the academy for a day? You get a reminder on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email). After 5 days without using the portal the account is suspended.

## The weekly townhall

**Me** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call''s deck, the next call time and its link. **Add to my calendar** adds the call every week.

## The weekly townhall (release 35)

Every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open **Townhall**: **Join the call** there, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.

## KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)

**KPIs by week** sits on **My scorecard**: your role''s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.

## Your schedule, hours and pay

**Hours** > **Schedule** shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.

| Role | Schedule |
| --- | --- |
| Customer service | 6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off |
| Finance | Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work |
| Fleet | 6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off |

1. Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.
2. You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under **Hours** > **My hours**, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.
3. Finance prepares the payroll under **Hours** > **Payroll**: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then **Send for approval**. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.

## The townhall''s 30 minutes

The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press **Join now** (from 15 minutes before), then **Confirm I am in the call** on the Townhall page, or press **Check in**: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? **Tell yours** under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week''s recording is listed on the Townhall page.

> Watch out: Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.

## Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)

- Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval.
- Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.
- Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.
- Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.

## The weekly townhall card (release 41)

From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the **Townhall** card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, **Join / check in** (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), **Add to calendar**, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.

## The townhall call in the site (release 50)

The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press **Join the call** on **Townhall** or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then **Join the call** again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.

- **Mute**, **Camera off** and **Leave** are under the video; **Share screen** on a computer.
- **Slides** beside the video follow the presenter. **Previous** and **Next** let you look on your own; **Back to the presenter** catches up.
- **Raise hand** to speak, **Chat** to write to everyone (not kept after the call).
- If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and **Join the call** opens that instead.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every function works the same way: start on To do, take the oldest task, finish it, and check Today for pickups and returns. The menu keeps your own work first, then the screens of your function in a few groups.</p><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-menu" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The menu</h2><p class="gd-p">Every office role has the same short menu: <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> (your home; Today at a glance is its second tab; problems in your work that the nightly Data health check found show there too), at most five links for your role, the last one <b class="gd-ui">More</b> for the rest of your work, <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> (Bookings, Calendar, Find a car, Find a renter, Card coverage) and <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> (My numbers: Scorecard and My sales; Academy). Actions are buttons on their page: <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New quote</b> on Requests, <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> on Bookings. Bookings opens on Now for every role (Sales without the money or the renters&#39; phones). Your group is always open. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button.</p><p class="gd-p">A <b class="gd-ui">More</b> page and a page with several parts open with a row on top (and a second row of tabs where a page has them). You see only the pages of your function.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Function</th><th scope="col">Your links, then More</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer service</td><td>Requests, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Messages. More customer service: Renters (Messages, Review requests, Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads, Owner pipeline, Owner forms), Listings (Listings, Similar cars), Chauffeur</td></tr><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Requests and offers, Visitors (Live now, Chat, History), Marketplace, My sales. More sales: Renters (Leads), Owners (Owner and buyer leads; your owners are on My sales), Chauffeur</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet</td><td>Field jobs, Fleet map, Checks (Daily checks, Photo reviews), Maintenance. More fleet: Field jobs (Jobs, Field hours), Listings (Listings, Similar cars, Calendar sync, Add-ons; Add a car for an owner is a button)</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Money (To handle, By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Reconciliation), Owner money (Invoices, Statements), Tolls and tickets, Turo trips. More finance: Maintenance bills</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-to-do" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">To do</h2><p class="gd-p">Tasks come to your function on their own: new requests, renter replies, failed payments, toll notices and more. To do puts the most urgent first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The top shows your function, today&#39;s date, how many things need you, your open, overdue and done-today figures, and your quickest actions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Next up</b> is the one task to do now. Press its button to do it, or <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your lanes group the work, for example Booking requests, Renter messages, Texts and calls, Live chat and Offers out. Each shows how many are waiting and how long the oldest has waited. Replies are timed against the 5-minute first reply target: past it the time turns red and says late. The most urgent lane comes first; press a lane to open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service and Sales: <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for a reply</b> lists every request, renter message, missed call and chat, the longest wait first, each with its reply button. Sales also sees the commission ring and Follow-ups due, Fleet today&#39;s handovers, returns and moves and the cars right now, Finance Money today.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Every open task</b>: filter All, Mine, Unassigned or Waiting. Under More filters: Any time, Overdue, Due today or Escalated, and by type. Each row has a priority, the task, its record, when it is due and a live timer of how long it has waited.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours. Pressing the task opens the screen where it is done: a chat waiting for a person opens that chat, documents to check open the review, a request opens the booking. <b class="gd-ui">Sheet</b> opens the step-by-step procedure.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Tasks close by themselves when their work is done elsewhere (an invoice paid or voided, a chat answered or closed); a day&#39;s opening and closing checks close at the end of that day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">On a computer, press <b class="gd-ui">/</b> to search (Find a renter; Sales: Find a car).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/940"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-01-queue-desktop-702d7c14.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="940"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:20.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.9%;top:52.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:72.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-work-a-task" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work a task</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the task. The buttons along the top move it on.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Button</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Open the working screen</b></td><td>Jumps to the booking, car or owner the task is about.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Done</b></td><td>You finished it. It leaves the queue.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b></td><td>You are waiting on someone (a renter, an owner). It stays yours.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Escalate</b></td><td>It needs an Admin. Add why.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Hand over</b></td><td>Give it to someone else on the team.</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b></td><td>Leave a note for whoever looks next.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Work oldest due first. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time; that is what your scorecard counts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-today" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Today</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Today lists pickups and returns, and what is due, for your function.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press a booking number to open it. <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> takes you back to your tasks.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/today</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/700"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-02-today-desktop-dfd277b7.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="700"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:24.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-documents-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Documents to sign</h2><p class="gd-p">Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The queue shows &quot;You have a document to sign&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values at the top (your role, hours, rate and start date), then press <b class="gd-ui">Read the PDF</b> and read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: press <b class="gd-ui">Send the code</b> and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b>. Several documents? One signature covers all of them. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-several-functions-switch-with-working-as" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Several functions? Switch with Working as</h2><p class="gd-p">If you cover more than one function, <b class="gd-ui">Working as</b> above the menu lists them: Customer service, Finance, Fleet and Sales. Choose one; the menu, To do and Today change to that function.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-your-scorecard" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your scorecard</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> (the <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b> tab).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure, its target and your result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The first reply target is 5 minutes: a new booking request, an enquiry, a change the renter asked for or a renter message is due 5 minutes after it comes in. An Admin sets it in Program settings, and the target column shows the one in force.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/360"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-78ec1b03.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="360"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.2%;top:39.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:62.5%;top:58.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-clock-in-and-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Clock in and out</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service, Fleet and Finance: press <b class="gd-ui">Clock in</b> on your home page when you start and <b class="gd-ui">Clock out</b> when you stop. <b class="gd-ui">My hours</b> shows today, the week and every entry. You are reminded if you have not clocked in 15 minutes after your start time.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-breaks-and-activity-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Breaks and activity (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Take breaks when you need them: there is no fixed length. Press <b class="gd-ui">Start break</b> next to the clock (a reason is optional) and <b class="gd-ui">End break</b> when you are back. The timer shows how long the break has run; after 30 minutes you get a reminder and the Admins see it. Clocking out ends a break. Your breaks are on <b class="gd-ui">My hours</b>; only an Admin can change one, with the reason.</p><p class="gd-p">While you are clocked in and not on a break, the portal notes that you are active: a click, a key, a scroll or switching to its tab. It never records what you type, which pages you open or your screen. Keep the portal open in a tab while you work; a hidden tab nobody touches counts as inactive. After a few minutes without activity it asks <b class="gd-ui">Still there?</b>: tap anywhere to carry on. Phone calls you take or make (your Quo user, the <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button or a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall count as active. Nothing is counted outside your scheduled hours.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-your-first-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first days</h2><p class="gd-p">Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first (sign it on Welcome or Documents to sign), then the academy, then everything else. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and your home page show your WhatsApp groups (Sales: CARMA Closers and the CarmaCars Team; everyone else the Team group). Next to each link is your member tag, written for you as &quot;Name - Position&quot; (for example &quot;Darren - Sales&quot;), with <b class="gd-ui">Copy member tag</b> and the steps: open the group, tap its name, tap your own name (or Edit member tag), paste and save. Join each group and set the tag, then press <b class="gd-ui">I joined</b> and tick <b class="gd-ui">I set my member tag</b>: I joined does not go through without it.</p><p class="gd-p">Passed the Sales part of the academy while Sales is not your main role? Your home page shows the Sales group (CARMA Closers) too: join it and set your tag the same way.</p><p class="gd-p">No progress in the academy for a day? You get a reminder on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email). After 5 days without using the portal the account is suspended.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call&#39;s deck, the next call time and its link. <b class="gd-ui">Add to my calendar</b> adds the call every week.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> there, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-kpis-on-your-scorecard-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">KPIs on your scorecard (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">KPIs by week</b> sits on <b class="gd-ui">My scorecard</b>: your role&#39;s KPIs against their targets (Program settings). Customer service: first reply within 5 minutes, conversations, licences reviewed, requests answered. Fleet: handovers on time, photo reviews, the next-day list, field jobs dispatched, calls. Finance: deposits reviewed in time, statements and invoices on time, tolls and tickets checked 2 to 3 times a week. A figure in red missed its target.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-your-schedule-hours-and-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your schedule, hours and pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b> shows your days and hours (Toronto) and who is working today. Breaks are at your discretion.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Schedule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Customer service</td><td>6 days a week, 8:00 am to 6:00 pm, Tuesday off</td></tr><tr><td>Finance</td><td>Monday, Wednesday and Friday plus the 10th and the 15th of each month, 10:00 am to 7:00 pm; one extra day a week when there is overflow work</td></tr><tr><td>Fleet</td><td>6 days a week, 11:00 am to 9:00 pm, Sunday off</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Clock in when you start and out when you stop. A clock-in more than 10 minutes after your start counts as late.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You are paid every two weeks: your monthly salary x 12 / 26. Your pay stubs are under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My hours</b>, each with its PDF, once an Admin approves the payroll.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Finance prepares the payroll under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payroll</b>: start it once the period has ended, add any bonus or deduction with its reason, then <b class="gd-ui">Send for approval</b>. An Admin approves it and records the payments; nothing is paid by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-townhall-s-30-minutes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall&#39;s 30 minutes</h2><p class="gd-p">The call link is at the top of your menu on every page. Press <b class="gd-ui">Join now</b> (from 15 minutes before), then <b class="gd-ui">Confirm I am in the call</b> on the Townhall page, or press <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b>: either counts you as there. Cameras on. Something wild happened this week? <b class="gd-ui">Tell yours</b> under Craziest story of the week: an Admin picks one for the deck. Each week&#39;s recording is listed on the Townhall page.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Two townhalls missed in a row lock your account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, or an Admin cancelled it) counts nobody absent, and a cancelled one sends no reminders.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-breaks-quiet-hours-and-the-approval-gate-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Breaks, quiet hours and the approval gate (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your portal opens after four steps: your staff agreement, the academy, the WhatsApp groups, then an Admin&#39;s or a Fleet VA&#39;s approval.</li><li>Log a break from your home page when you step away, and end it when you are back. While you are on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused. Otherwise, a long time with no activity on your shift sends you an alert, then the Admins.</li><li>Quiet hours: alerts held by your quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end. Renters get no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning.</li><li>Your schedule, pay stubs (every two weeks) and KPIs are on your home page and My hours. The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock your account.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-weekly-townhall-card-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall card (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, <b class="gd-ui">Join / check in</b> (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-workday-the-townhall-call-in-the-site-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall call in the site (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Camera off</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Leave</b> are under the video; <b class="gd-ui">Share screen</b> on a computer.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Slides</b> beside the video follow the presenter. <b class="gd-ui">Previous</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> let you look on your own; <b class="gd-ui">Back to the presenter</b> catches up.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Raise hand</b> to speak, <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> to write to everyone (not kept after the call).</li><li>If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens that instead.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'sales', 'chapter', 'fleet', 'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.
6. To look again at an image already approved or rejected, press **View** beside it (it opens for one minute and the view is logged). After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do "Expired offer: win the renter back" (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter''s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 12 hours (never past 1 hour before the pickup) unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Leads and claims

Open **Leads**. Every lead is there: renter leads (forms, live chat, the phone number box, games, expired offers, requests not sent, missed calls, Live visitors), owner leads and partner leads, new and hot first. A new-lead alert on your phone opens that lead.

1. Press **Next lead**, or **Claim** on a card. The lead is yours for 15 minutes.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**: your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged. Each contact (or **Note**) adds 15 minutes, up to 60 minutes from your claim.
3. Press **Outcome**: Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won or Lost (say why). Or **Mark handled** when there is nothing more to do.
4. Can''t finish? Press **Unclaim** so someone else can take it. A claim that runs out goes back to the pool by itself.

You hold at most 25 leads at once. Your numbers are on To do under **My leads**: leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week and this month. Owner leads are also under **Owners** > **Leads**.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

Press **The person** on a lead card, or open the lead, to see everything we know about them in one place: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, account and whether the licence is verified (yes or no, never the number), every booking with the car, dates, status, total and anything owed, the deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, and who has handled them. **Signals** lists everything they did with us, newest first: calls and texts, WhatsApp, chat, emails, visits, cars and offers looked at, bookings and reviews. The intent score counts all of it.

When the renter is outside your window, you see their contact and account until the lead is yours: claim it (or an Admin assigns it to you) and the rest opens, logged as a record you opened for a reason. An Admin can assign leads to you in bulk: they show **Assigned to you by an Admin**, do not run out, and do not count against your limit of open leads.
## Call minutes (release 35)
Your home shows **My call minutes**: today, this week and this month, for connected calls made with the site''s **Call** button. Customer numbers are hidden for Sales; call and text with the buttons on the page.


## Get a renter ready for the pickup (release 35)
Your work does not stop at the offer. Until the car is handed over you can do everything that gets the renter good to go:
- **Payment**: send a pay link or a deposit link on Money (text or email), or take the card on this device, also on a confirmed booking.
- **The offer**: edit it, send it again with a later expiry, withdraw it or record that the renter approved by phone, also while it waits for payment.
- **ID and coverage**: approve or reject the licence, the selfie and the proof of coverage, with the reason the renter sees.
- **Drivers and agreement**: send each additional driver their signing link, or the agreement again.
- **Name change asked for**: when a verified renter asks for a name or date of birth correction, it shows on the booking; check it against the licence, then **Approve** or **Decline**.

The booking page shows **Ready for the rental**: one line for each thing the pickup needs (offer accepted, paid, licence and selfie, coverage, deposit, drivers, agreement, add-ons in the car), green when done, with what to press when not. Refunds, cancellations, deposit releases and removing a paid add-on stay with customer service, Finance and Admins.

## The Prepare checklist (release 35)
On a booking with add-ons, **Prepare for the pickup** shows each add-on with its quantity, ticked or not by field staff, who ticked it and when, and the pickup or delivery job with its field person. It is on the booking and on the car page, for Sales, customer service, Fleet and Finance.

## Rebooking, intent and offers (release 35)

- A returning renter''s new request comes straight to you when you had their last booking, with the usual claim time.
- Each lead shows its intent (hot, warm or cold) and what the person said they want, read from calls with their transcripts, texts, emails, chat and visits. Call hot leads first.
- Offers are three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every version is kept; you can load an old one as a new offer.
- Prices stay between the owner''s daily minimum and maximum; only an Admin allows one outside them.
- Verified renters with the Gold Rewards tier or above can book instantly; their booking is marked Instant (repeat renter).
- Rewards: tell renters they earn points for a photo with their review and every rental after the first.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead customer service is handling (release 37)

When customer service or Fleet are on a call with a lead, the lead and the lists say **Being handled by** their first name, their function and the time. Leave it alone: you cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome, and **Next lead** skips it. When their time ends, the lead returns to you if you had a claim on it or brought it, else to the open list. The booking credit rules do not change.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## A request that did not go through (release 42)

A **Request did not go through** To-do means a customer pressed Send request and it was refused or failed. The To-do has their name, email, phone, the car, the dates and the reason they were shown.

1. Call or text them soon: they wanted to book.
2. Their answers are still in the form on their device. Tell them what to change (the reason says which field), or make the offer yourself with **New quote**.
3. When their request arrives, the To-do closes by itself. If they no longer want the car, complete it with a note.

An urgent one means our system could not take the request: the customer was told we will contact them, so contact them first.

## A lead''s phone number (release 46)

Customer numbers show with dots in place of most digits. **Call** and **Text** still reach the person through the business number.

1. Need the whole number of one lead (to give it at the counter or to dial it yourself)? On the lead, press **Ask an Admin to show the number**. An Admin gets a To do on that lead; asking again adds no second one.
2. When an Admin shows it to you, the lead says **Number shown by an Admin**: the full number, with a call link and **Copy**, on that lead only: its page, its card in the list and its calls. You also get an alert that opens the lead. Every other lead stays hidden, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone).
3. If the lead goes to another salesperson, the number is hidden from you again by itself, and the new salesperson sees it hidden until an Admin shows it to them.

## Where a lead came from (release 48)

Every lead card and every lead''s page says where the person came from, for forms and requests sent from the website.

1. On a lead card, the badge under the source reads for example "ChatGPT", "Google search", "Google Ads", "Perplexity", "Bing" or "Direct (typed or bookmarked)", with the search terms when we have them and "First page" (the first page they opened on the site).
2. On the lead''s page, the card **Where they came from** lists: **Came from**, **Search terms**, **First page they opened**, **Page of the latest visit**, **Referring page** and **Campaign**. A row we do not know is left out.
3. Search terms come from the ad or campaign link, or from the search page they came from (Bing and DuckDuckGo sometimes send them). Google does not send the words searched: for a Google visit the card lists the top Google searches that bring people to that first page, from Search Console.
4. Use it in the first call: someone who came from "kill switch for car" wants the tracker; someone who landed on a monthly rental page wants a monthly price.

> Good to know: a call, a chat and a lead typed by staff have no source, and the card says so. Leads from before release 48 have none either.

## Duplicate leads (release 48)

The same person often writes twice: the contact form, then the chat, then a call. Your lead list keeps them as one, so two people never call the same person.

1. A new website form from someone who already has an open lead of the same kind (same email or same phone, in the last 14 days) joins that lead by itself. Its message shows on the older lead under "Also wrote", marked "merged automatically".
2. A lead with another lead of the same person shows "possible duplicate: merge" on its card. Open it: the card "Possible duplicates" lists each one with why it matches (same email, same phone, same browser).
3. Press **Merge**. The oldest lead is kept. The other''s message, calls, texts, chats and notes move to it, and the other is closed as merged. Nothing is deleted.
4. **Merge all into the oldest** does every duplicate at once.
5. Two people who share an email or a phone (a couple, an office line): press **Different person**. The pair is never suggested again.
6. A renter lead and an owner lead of the same person stay apart: they are different conversations.

> Good to know: a lead that was already handled is not reopened by a new form. The new form is a new lead, with the merge offered, so you decide.

## Renter sent an e-Transfer (release 49)

You cannot record a payment; Finance does. When a renter says they sent the e-Transfer on a booking waiting for payment:

1. Open the booking, the **Money** tab, then **Renter sent an e-Transfer**.
2. Type the amount sent, choose what it covers (**The rental and fees**, **The deposit** or **Both**), the sender''s name if you have it, and add the screenshot or proof (a photo or a PDF). **Send to Finance**.
3. Nothing is marked paid. The booking shows **e-Transfer reported, waiting for Finance** and Finance gets a Check e-Transfer To do.
4. You are told when Finance answers: confirmed (the payment is recorded and the booking confirmed), or not received with their reason. Then check with the renter and report it again.
5. One report waits at a time on a booking.

### Owner pipeline: move an owner forward

Owners, then **Owner pipeline**, shows your owners'' cars (customer service and Fleet: every owner''s) by step: days in the step, the next action and whose turn it is. Red cards are stalled (3 days or more): you also get a To do.

1. Start with the card that waited longest. Open **Call script** and call the owner: the script fits their step.
2. No answer? Press **Nudge**: a CarmaCars email and text with their next step, what to bring and how long it takes (once in 10 minutes a car).
3. Open the owner to see each car''s steps and the blockers. You can enter the ServiceOntario appointment for them; Fleet records the visit, the fleet policy and the inspection.
', 'Sales', 'Requests and offers, new quotes and owner leads.',
  'You turn enquiries into bookings and owners into fleet: requests and offers, quotes for callers, and owner leads.

> Good to know: Leads come to you only once you pass the academy (or an Admin waives it) and finish onboarding. Until then you get no lead alert, cannot claim a lead or be given one, and Leads stays closed.

Your menu: To do, Today, My scorecard and My sales, then Requests and offers, Send an offer, Add a rental, New quote, Calendar and Buyer leads. The owners you bring in are on My sales.

## Requests, offers and new quotes

1. **Requests and offers**: the same queue customer service works, showing only what you can answer now. A request still with customer service is folded under "more not open to you yet", with the time it opens to you.
2. **Rentals** > **Bookings**: **My bookings**, every booking credited to you, offered by you or added by you, from the offer to the return, with its status, money and your commission (counting this month, waiting for approval, approved, paid).
3. **Send an offer**: one screen for a caller, sent at once, as in chapter 2. **New quote** still makes a request to offer later.
3. An offer that is out: **More actions** > **Edit the offer**, then **Send the update**.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-02-requests-desktop-2ab1d17d.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 580; address: carmacars.ca/va/requests; pins: 1 39.8 59.5")

> Tip: Your first reply target is 5 minutes, the "Quote sent" measure on your scorecard. Follow every offer out before it expires.

## Check the renter''s licence

Sales approve the renter''s licence like customer service: the licence front, the licence back and the selfie. The proof of coverage and the Protection Plan stay with customer service and Admins.

1. On **To do**, **Licences to check** lists each booking with an image waiting, the longest wait first. Press **Review the licence**.
2. On a booking, the card **Renter licence** has the same: press **Review the licence**.
3. Look at each image and each Flag line of the licence reader under the driver: no alteration, the selfie matches the licence photo.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told and asked for a new image.
5. Then press **Approve all**: every image still waiting is approved at once. An image the system refuses is named with the reason.
6. To look again at an image already approved or rejected, press **View** beside it (it opens for one minute and the view is logged). After the 90-day removal it reads **Removed on** and the date.

> Tip: The booking history says who decided and the role, sales. Each opening of the images is logged and the links last one minute.

## In person or remote

Every Sales person works in one of two modes, on the same Sales screens. An Admin sets yours; it shows at the top of To do and on My sales.

|  | In person (Toronto) | Remote (anywhere) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Commission | Under 50 rental days in the month 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20% | Under 50 rental days 5%, from 50 days 10%, from 100 days 15% |
| Credit | Walk-ins, handovers you close, partner visits and the rentals you source | Only the rentals you source. A website request you answer with the first offer during one of your blocks counts as yours. Walk-ins and partner deals earn nothing |
| Hours | You choose | At least 20 hours a week of Thursday to Sunday afternoons (noon to 6 pm, Toronto time), replying within 15 minutes to the chats, texts and calls assigned to you |
| Every day | Nothing set | Marketplace and classified reposts, social media DM replies, three follow-ups on every quote, long-term and business outreach |
| Every month | Nothing set | 400 touches. Under 400 when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower: 15% becomes 10%, 10% becomes 5%, 5% becomes 2.5% |

## Remote: your duties

On **To do**, **Remote duties** shows this month''s touches against 400, today''s checklist, the peak hours you scheduled this week and your reply time.

1. Most touches count by themselves: an offer you send, a message or text you send from the portal, a live chat you answer (once a day for each chat), a call or text from the phone line, an ad you post, a call or message to a car owner.
2. For anything else press **Log a touch**: choose the type and add the link of the post, profile or listing if there is one.
3. The checklist ticks itself as the day''s touches come in. Three follow-ups on every quote stays open while a deal of yours has fewer than three.
4. Under My availability choose this week or next, press **Add a block** for each time you will be on, then **Save the week**. Days already past stay as they were.
5. A website request you answer with the first offer during a block is credited to you as sourced, even if you chose Entered for CarmaCars. Off your blocks it stays a claim for an Admin.

> Tip: An Admin can void a touch logged by mistake. Once an Admin approves a month, its mode, its rates and its touches no longer change; a refund can still lower the tier, as for everyone.

## My sales

Open **Me**, the **My sales** tab. It shows your own sales and commissions only.

1. Commissions comes first. Your rate depends on your mode and the rental days of the month: in person 10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100; remote 5%, 10% and 15%. The bar shows your days against the target of 100, and says when your rate rises. By month gives each month in one line: the mode, the days, the rate and, for remote, the touches and any drop.
2. The tiles show this week: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press **By month** for months, **By week** for weeks.
3. By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.
4. Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.
5. Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to you | A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else. |
| Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added | Counted on the day they happened. |
| Bookings confirmed, booked revenue | Counted on the day the booking was confirmed. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |
| Rental days (Sales) | The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month''s tier applies to all of that month''s rentals. |

> Tip: Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month''s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.

## Owners you bring in

Bring in car owners on **My work** > **My sales**, card **Owners you bring in**. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as "sourced by", with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.

1. **Invite an owner**: enter their name, email and phone, tick **The owner asked me to send it**, then press **Send the invitation**. They get an email with your link to apply.
2. **Copy my owner link**: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.
3. **Start an application**: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin''s. A corporation that leases its cars to CarmaCars: choose **A corporation**, then Route **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**, and each car''s tier (**Regular** or **Troubled**). A fleet supplier can also apply himself from `carmacars.ca/list-your-car`: your owner link works for it too.
4. The row of five figures follows your owners: **Invited**, **Applied**, **Approved**, **Car live** and **First paid rental**. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.

5. Someone who starts the application on the website and stops for 30 minutes comes to you: a task "Unfinished owner application" and their row on My sales (Lead). Call or text them; the follow-up emails go by themselves until they finish.

> Tip: An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.

## Ask for your commission on an owner

There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.

1. On the owner''s row press **Ask for a commission**.
2. Choose **A flat amount** and type it, or **A percent**: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company''s share of their cars'' rentals, or their cars'' rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).
3. Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press **Send to an Admin**.
4. While it waits you can press **Change my request**. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.

| Approved as | When it is earned |
| --- | --- |
| A flat amount | Once, at the owner''s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full |
| A percent | On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved |

> Tip: Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars'' own cars, a partner''s, a shareholder''s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.

## Buyer leads

1. **Buyer leads**: each request from the /buy pages, with the car, budget and timing.
2. Press **Take it** to make it yours, then call them.
3. Press **Update** to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.

> Tip: Owner leads are not here. The owners you invite or add are on **My sales**, **Owners you bring in**, and you see only your own. Customer service works the full owner pipeline.

An offer that has been expired for 7 days leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead: you get the To do "Expired offer: win the renter back" (the lead goes to the Sales person with the fewest open leads) with the renter''s contact, the car and the dates they wanted. Call or text them, then mark the lead contacted or closed.

**Reopen offer** on an expired booking (or the **Expired** filter of Requests) sends the offer again in one click, open 12 hours (never past 1 hour before the pickup) unless you set the hours; a pickup time that has passed asks for new dates first. "Renter wants expired offer reopened" To dos come from the renter''s own button. The offer screens block **Send** with **Pickup time has passed: update it** until the pickup is moved.

## Book it now (release 33)
When you send an offer, tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** when the renter has already agreed. The offer goes out and an Admin approves it in one tap: the booking then waits for payment, the car is held, and the renter gets one link to sign and pay. You can also have them sign and pay with you: open the booking, **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device.
Already sent the offer? Ask the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the customer agreed by phone". It shows a card; **Confirm** sends the same request to an Admin, who approves in one tap.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Leads and claims

Open **Leads**. Every lead is there: renter leads (forms, live chat, the phone number box, games, expired offers, requests not sent, missed calls, Live visitors), owner leads and partner leads, new and hot first. A new-lead alert on your phone opens that lead.

1. Press **Next lead**, or **Claim** on a card. The lead is yours for 15 minutes.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**: your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged. Each contact (or **Note**) adds 15 minutes, up to 60 minutes from your claim.
3. Press **Outcome**: Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won or Lost (say why). Or **Mark handled** when there is nothing more to do.
4. Can''t finish? Press **Unclaim** so someone else can take it. A claim that runs out goes back to the pool by itself.

You hold at most 25 leads at once. Your numbers are on To do under **My leads**: leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week and this month. Owner leads are also under **Owners** > **Leads**.

## The person behind the lead (release 40)

Press **The person** on a lead card, or open the lead, to see everything we know about them in one place: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, account and whether the licence is verified (yes or no, never the number), every booking with the car, dates, status, total and anything owed, the deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents, and who has handled them. **Signals** lists everything they did with us, newest first: calls and texts, WhatsApp, chat, emails, visits, cars and offers looked at, bookings and reviews. The intent score counts all of it.

When the renter is outside your window, you see their contact and account until the lead is yours: claim it (or an Admin assigns it to you) and the rest opens, logged as a record you opened for a reason. An Admin can assign leads to you in bulk: they show **Assigned to you by an Admin**, do not run out, and do not count against your limit of open leads.
## Call minutes (release 35)
Your home shows **My call minutes**: today, this week and this month, for connected calls made with the site''s **Call** button. Customer numbers are hidden for Sales; call and text with the buttons on the page.


## Get a renter ready for the pickup (release 35)
Your work does not stop at the offer. Until the car is handed over you can do everything that gets the renter good to go:
- **Payment**: send a pay link or a deposit link on Money (text or email), or take the card on this device, also on a confirmed booking.
- **The offer**: edit it, send it again with a later expiry, withdraw it or record that the renter approved by phone, also while it waits for payment.
- **ID and coverage**: approve or reject the licence, the selfie and the proof of coverage, with the reason the renter sees.
- **Drivers and agreement**: send each additional driver their signing link, or the agreement again.
- **Name change asked for**: when a verified renter asks for a name or date of birth correction, it shows on the booking; check it against the licence, then **Approve** or **Decline**.

The booking page shows **Ready for the rental**: one line for each thing the pickup needs (offer accepted, paid, licence and selfie, coverage, deposit, drivers, agreement, add-ons in the car), green when done, with what to press when not. Refunds, cancellations, deposit releases and removing a paid add-on stay with customer service, Finance and Admins.

## The Prepare checklist (release 35)
On a booking with add-ons, **Prepare for the pickup** shows each add-on with its quantity, ticked or not by field staff, who ticked it and when, and the pickup or delivery job with its field person. It is on the booking and on the car page, for Sales, customer service, Fleet and Finance.

## Rebooking, intent and offers (release 35)

- A returning renter''s new request comes straight to you when you had their last booking, with the usual claim time.
- Each lead shows its intent (hot, warm or cold) and what the person said they want, read from calls with their transcripts, texts, emails, chat and visits. Call hot leads first.
- Offers are three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every version is kept; you can load an old one as a new offer.
- Prices stay between the owner''s daily minimum and maximum; only an Admin allows one outside them.
- Verified renters with the Gold Rewards tier or above can book instantly; their booking is marked Instant (repeat renter).
- Rewards: tell renters they earn points for a photo with their review and every rental after the first.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead customer service is handling (release 37)

When customer service or Fleet are on a call with a lead, the lead and the lists say **Being handled by** their first name, their function and the time. Leave it alone: you cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome, and **Next lead** skips it. When their time ends, the lead returns to you if you had a claim on it or brought it, else to the open list. The booking credit rules do not change.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## A request that did not go through (release 42)

A **Request did not go through** To-do means a customer pressed Send request and it was refused or failed. The To-do has their name, email, phone, the car, the dates and the reason they were shown.

1. Call or text them soon: they wanted to book.
2. Their answers are still in the form on their device. Tell them what to change (the reason says which field), or make the offer yourself with **New quote**.
3. When their request arrives, the To-do closes by itself. If they no longer want the car, complete it with a note.

An urgent one means our system could not take the request: the customer was told we will contact them, so contact them first.

## A lead''s phone number (release 46)

Customer numbers show with dots in place of most digits. **Call** and **Text** still reach the person through the business number.

1. Need the whole number of one lead (to give it at the counter or to dial it yourself)? On the lead, press **Ask an Admin to show the number**. An Admin gets a To do on that lead; asking again adds no second one.
2. When an Admin shows it to you, the lead says **Number shown by an Admin**: the full number, with a call link and **Copy**, on that lead only: its page, its card in the list and its calls. You also get an alert that opens the lead. Every other lead stays hidden, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone).
3. If the lead goes to another salesperson, the number is hidden from you again by itself, and the new salesperson sees it hidden until an Admin shows it to them.

## Where a lead came from (release 48)

Every lead card and every lead''s page says where the person came from, for forms and requests sent from the website.

1. On a lead card, the badge under the source reads for example "ChatGPT", "Google search", "Google Ads", "Perplexity", "Bing" or "Direct (typed or bookmarked)", with the search terms when we have them and "First page" (the first page they opened on the site).
2. On the lead''s page, the card **Where they came from** lists: **Came from**, **Search terms**, **First page they opened**, **Page of the latest visit**, **Referring page** and **Campaign**. A row we do not know is left out.
3. Search terms come from the ad or campaign link, or from the search page they came from (Bing and DuckDuckGo sometimes send them). Google does not send the words searched: for a Google visit the card lists the top Google searches that bring people to that first page, from Search Console.
4. Use it in the first call: someone who came from "kill switch for car" wants the tracker; someone who landed on a monthly rental page wants a monthly price.

> Good to know: a call, a chat and a lead typed by staff have no source, and the card says so. Leads from before release 48 have none either.

## Duplicate leads (release 48)

The same person often writes twice: the contact form, then the chat, then a call. Your lead list keeps them as one, so two people never call the same person.

1. A new website form from someone who already has an open lead of the same kind (same email or same phone, in the last 14 days) joins that lead by itself. Its message shows on the older lead under "Also wrote", marked "merged automatically".
2. A lead with another lead of the same person shows "possible duplicate: merge" on its card. Open it: the card "Possible duplicates" lists each one with why it matches (same email, same phone, same browser).
3. Press **Merge**. The oldest lead is kept. The other''s message, calls, texts, chats and notes move to it, and the other is closed as merged. Nothing is deleted.
4. **Merge all into the oldest** does every duplicate at once.
5. Two people who share an email or a phone (a couple, an office line): press **Different person**. The pair is never suggested again.
6. A renter lead and an owner lead of the same person stay apart: they are different conversations.

> Good to know: a lead that was already handled is not reopened by a new form. The new form is a new lead, with the merge offered, so you decide.

## Renter sent an e-Transfer (release 49)

You cannot record a payment; Finance does. When a renter says they sent the e-Transfer on a booking waiting for payment:

1. Open the booking, the **Money** tab, then **Renter sent an e-Transfer**.
2. Type the amount sent, choose what it covers (**The rental and fees**, **The deposit** or **Both**), the sender''s name if you have it, and add the screenshot or proof (a photo or a PDF). **Send to Finance**.
3. Nothing is marked paid. The booking shows **e-Transfer reported, waiting for Finance** and Finance gets a Check e-Transfer To do.
4. You are told when Finance answers: confirmed (the payment is recorded and the booking confirmed), or not received with their reason. Then check with the renter and report it again.
5. One report waits at a time on a booking.

### Owner pipeline: move an owner forward

Owners, then **Owner pipeline**, shows your owners'' cars (customer service and Fleet: every owner''s) by step: days in the step, the next action and whose turn it is. Red cards are stalled (3 days or more): you also get a To do.

1. Start with the card that waited longest. Open **Call script** and call the owner: the script fits their step.
2. No answer? Press **Nudge**: a CarmaCars email and text with their next step, what to bring and how long it takes (once in 10 minutes a car).
3. Open the owner to see each car''s steps and the blockers. You can enter the ServiceOntario appointment for them; Fleet records the visit, the fleet policy and the inspection.
