 a renter signs.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>When we update our terms of use, our privacy policy or an agreement you signed with us, the next time you open your portal it shows <b class="gd-ui">We&#39;ve updated our terms</b>: a short summary of what changed and the new text. Tick that you read it and press <b class="gd-ui">Accept</b> to continue. It does not change an agreement you already signed or a past booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-your-first-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first days</h2><p class="gd-p">Your portal opens in order: your staff agreement first, then the academy (Training), then your jobs. Welcome shows each step and asks for the name you go by. Once both are done, Welcome and Today show the team&#39;s WhatsApp group: join it, then press <b class="gd-ui">I joined</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-the-weekly-townhall-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time, and everyone attends. Open <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> there, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts you as there. You get a reminder an hour before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-report-a-bug-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Report a bug (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Something not working? Press <b class="gd-ui">Report a bug</b> at the top of any page. A picture of the page is taken first (passwords and card fields are hidden); write what happened (at least 30 characters), what you expected and the steps if you know them, choose how bad it is (<b class="gd-ui">Blocks my work</b> alerts the Admins at once) and add or paste more pictures. The page, your browser and its recent errors go with it. <b class="gd-ui">My bug reports</b> shows each report and its status: new, being looked at, fixed or won&#39;t fix.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-the-weekly-townhall-card-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The weekly townhall card (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">From the day before the weekly townhall until it ends, your home page shows the <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> card: the day and time (Toronto), a countdown, <b class="gd-ui">Join / check in</b> (it opens 15 minutes before; joining through it checks you in), <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>, and a red line if you missed the last townhall: one more miss locks your account. You also get a reminder the day before at 10:00 am, the morning of at 9:00 am, an hour before, and 15 minutes before with the join link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-work-chats-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work chats only</h2><p class="gd-p">All work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. Questions, handovers, problems and customer details go in the group, so the whole team sees them and nothing is lost when someone is away. If a colleague or an Admin writes to you privately about work, answer in the group.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-something-to-check-on-your-record-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Something to check on your record (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When something on your record looks wrong, a box opens on any page of the portal and says exactly what, with the box to fix it right there: your staff agreement waiting for your driver&#39;s licence number or home address, a home address outside Ontario while you work in person in Toronto (fix it, or press It&#39;s correct and say why), a licence that expires within 30 days (or has expired), pay details missing, a phone number that is not valid, or your WhatsApp member tag not confirmed. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b> and the box checks again.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Your agreement waiting for something you give cannot be put off: once you save it, the agreement is made and appears under Documents to sign at once. The sign page says the same when nothing is ready to sign yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Anything else you can put off with <b class="gd-ui">Remind me later</b>: it comes back after a day.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-guide-me" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Guide me</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Guide me</b> walks you through a job step by step while you do it: a pickup, a return or an expense. Press <b class="gd-ui">Guide me</b> at the top (or <b class="gd-ui">Guide me: a pickup</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Guide me: a return</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Guide me: an expense</b> on Today). A card points at the next thing to do, with Step X of Y; it moves on by itself once you have done it. <b class="gd-ui">Back</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Skip</b> and the cross (exit) are always there, and it picks up where you were if you leave the page. Tick <b class="gd-ui">Keep Guide me on</b> to have it offer each time.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-the-townhall-call-in-the-site-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall call in the site (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">The weekly townhall is a video call inside the portal: no outside link to open. An email brings you the calendar invite once (it repeats every week, Toronto time) and updates it by itself when the day or time changes. From 15 minutes before, press <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b> or on the Townhall card, allow your camera and microphone, then <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> again. Being in the call counts your attendance by itself: the time you joined and left is recorded.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Camera off</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Leave</b> are under the video; <b class="gd-ui">Share screen</b> on a computer.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Slides</b> beside the video follow the presenter. <b class="gd-ui">Previous</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> let you look on your own; <b class="gd-ui">Back to the presenter</b> catches up.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Raise hand</b> to speak, <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> to write to everyone (not kept after the call).</li><li>If the call in the site is down, an Admin switches the townhall to the outside link and <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens that instead.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'academy', 'chapter', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.

1. Open **Academy** and the first open section.
2. Press **Play** on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone''s own voice. **Pause**, **Back**, **Next**, **Replay** and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves. Each section ends with a lesson called **See it**: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs.
3. Answer the quiz and press **Check my answers**. Every question has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong. 80% passes and opens the next section; **Try again** as often as you need. Until you pass your path, the rest of the portal waits (the guide and your profile stay open).

> Tip: Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**: welcome, then your profile and phone, then the academy, then your first tasks (press **Done** on each). Until you pass the academy, only Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile open.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%, opens after the reading time, waits 30 minutes after a failed try and allows 3 tries a day. You get field jobs only once you have passed and hold a shift that day.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Your training now has the path **The renter''s side**: what the renter sees at each step, from the request to the deposit back, with each page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your field path also has a section of worked examples from this guide: the ready check, the original licence, cash and add-ons.

1. New staff take both from the start. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date; after it, the rest of the portal waits until they are passed.
2. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on. Read it before you call the office.', 'Academy', 'Your training: watch the lessons on your phone, pass each quiz.',
  'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.

